  "lineage": "The solo and lead tradition of the Paraguayan diatonic harp, descended from Jesuit mission harps of the seventeenth-century Guaraní reductions and rebuilt in the twentieth century as a light 36-38 string cedar instrument played with fingernails, virtuosically codified by Félix Pérez Cardozo in the 1930s-40s and by Digno García and Luis Bordón after him — right-hand tremolo and glissando figuration over left-hand 3/4 bass in polca and galopa, with showpiece programmatic imitations such as Pájaro Campana.",
